1. She is British and often receives comments about her Britishness. (Verbatim: "you've missed my Britishness, fantastic, I rarely hear that because, it's more like, boo, she British, ew, oh dear")

2. She currently resides in the United States, not in England. (Verbatim: "sorry, I also have one screen, you may have guessed, I am still not in England, I am still in the wonderful land of the free")

3. She attended Anime Expo (AX) for two days and revealed her appearance there. (Verbatim: "I actually went to AX, I did, I didn't go all the days, um, I went for, for two of the days")

4. Her persona or 2D representation was drawn by Mozumi Peachy based on a photo of her. (Verbatim: "we can thank Mozumi Peachy for, for turning me into kind of a 2D-ish anime girl here, but it's just a direct, direct trace")

5. She refers to an outgoing alter ego named "Extrovert Ellie" who functions during events like conventions. (Verbatim: "Extrovert Ellie is the one that's been functioning and running this ship, um, for the times I was at AX")

6. She gets sick easily, often attributing illness to going outside. (Verbatim: "I get sick really easily, I'll be honest, I get, I think I just get sick from going outside")

7. She has a high tolerance for cringe and jokes about her cringe factor increasing. (Verbatim: "as you can see, I didn't get any less cringe while I was away, I'm still as cringe as always, in fact, you might say my cringe factor has increased")

8. She associates charisma with her British accent. (Verbatim: "Yes, the charisma all comes with the accent")

9. She enjoys drinking cola and Gatorade, particularly red and blue flavors. (Verbatim: "on one hand, I have cookie cola, on the other hand, I have gatorade" and "I've had a lot of blue flavored stuff over here, red for it is banned in the UK")

10. She streamed from her bed while sick, indicating a habit of streaming despite illness out of dedication to her audience. (Verbatim: "sorry, I'm actually streaming from bed, um, so that is why, this will be going fantastic, there is a possibility I'll just fall asleep") [end of text]



1. She has a tendency to get sick with congestion and difficulty breathing through her nose. (Verbatim: "i've been on that one nostril breathing life for a while... the left one for now")
2. She refers to herself as "sick Elia" when unwell, indicating a self-aware persona shift during illness. (Verbatim: "sick elia is barely functioning like struggles struggling functioning")
3. She believes having a fever is a sign her body is fighting, and views it positively. (Verbatim: "fever is good fever means i'm fighting yo")
4. She created and released a yandere-themed rap before leaving for America. (Verbatim: "i released that yandere rap... just before... i want america i am i rap")
5. She experiences anxiety and insecurity despite feeling inspired and determined. (Verbatim: "i'm filled with so much determination... but just equal amounts of insecurity and anxiety")
6. She drinks a tea she jokingly calls "anxiety" and consumes caffeine regularly. (Verbatim: "anxiety my favorite tea... all i need and caffeine")
7. She has traveled to America and noticed an increase in Cybertrucks there. (Verbatim: "i've seen tons of that... i didn't see one before i may see")
8. She mentions the rabies vaccine only slows the virus to allow time for treatment, indicating knowledge or interest in medical facts. (Verbatim: "the rabies vaccine doesn't actually protect you from rabies it just slows it down enough to give you a chance")
9. She has a recurring self-deprecating theme, stating she is "nothing special" despite wanting to bring joy. (Verbatim: "i'm not great i wish i was great i'm nothing special")
10. She jokes about creating absurd merch, including "moonshine," "bathwater," and "wisdom tuff," suggesting a surreal humor style. (Verbatim: "So we add this to my new merch list... Moonshine. Bathwater... my wisdom tuff.") [end of text]



1. She has a recurring nightmare where she is lost in a large building with many doors and rooms. (Verbatim: "I keep having a dream where I'm, like, stuck in this building and there's all these doors and I can't find my way out and running around.")
2. She suffers from recurring dreams, including ones set in a place similar to the village where she grew up. (Verbatim: "I've had a few recurring dreams there. School's probably the worst one.")
3. She frequently has recurring school-related dreams, which she finds distressing. (Verbatim: "I always have recurring school dreams.")
4. She dislikes nightmares and is hesitant to sleep because of them. (Verbatim: "I don't know if I want to sleep. If I sleep- if I sleep I'll have nightmares and I don't like having nightmares.")
5. She identifies as a shy person and found it difficult to post a cosplay photo publicly. (Verbatim: "I'm a shy person so posting that was really hard.")
6. She once wrote a social media post but delayed posting it for a long time due to nervousness. (Verbatim: "I actually wrote the post and I didn't actually post it for ages... I was so nervous so nervous.")
7. She attended Anime Expo and had fun there, including cosplaying. (Verbatim: "maybe I had a good time at ax... glad you had fun during the anime expo.")
8. She dislikes being sick because it prevents her from working and feels boring. (Verbatim: "I hate being sick being six socks and it's boring and I want to work I can't work if I'm sick.")
9. She enjoys tacos and expressed a craving for them. (Verbatim: "I want tacos i want tacos tacos.")
10. She naps frequently, sometimes as a result of overworking and exhaustion. (Verbatim: "I'm someone that naps a lot but sometimes I think I just overwork and exhaust myself.") [end of text]



1. She describes her origin lore as a winged messenger from above who was hit by a truck in the sky and reincarnated as a British girl. (Verbatim: "until i got hit by trucking in the sky and got reincarnated as a british girl wild right absolutely wild lore")

2. She is British and references UK-specific culture, such as Tesco and the absence of raccoons in England. (Verbatim: "meet me behind Tesco" / "no, no, they don't have them in England, that is why I need to find one")

3. She identifies herself as a tomboy during childhood and often wore boy clothes due to having two older brothers and hand-me-downs. (Verbatim: "I think I was a tomboy for real... put her in boy clothes")

4. She was not allowed to have long hair as a child because it was difficult to take care of. (Verbatim: "my parents wouldn't let me have long hair... it was difficult to take care of")

5. She has two brothers and grew up fighting them with sticks; she was not allowed a lightsaber toy because she broke things with it. (Verbatim: "most of my memories of my brothers growing up was just fighting them... I broke stuff with it accidentally")

6. She now enjoys girly things as an adult because she was restricted from them in childhood. (Verbatim: "why do you think I really like girly things now, I'm free to have all the happy girly things")

7. She has a self-described "short person energy" and jokes about her height, denying being four feet tall but confirming she is not very tall. (Verbatim: "short person energy where huh you hate you whooped me" / "I'm not five foot one" / "I'm not actually that short like hello")

8. She expresses a fascination with raccoons and wants fans to bring her one, preferably alive. (Verbatim: "if you give me one raccoon one raccoon one forgiveness... preferably alive")

9. She does not have a manager and handles all aspects of her VTuber work herself. (Verbatim: "i don't have a manager like yeah yeah yeah yeah i be doing all my things yeah yeah yeah yeah i am the manager")

10. She struggles with self-doubt and emotional exhaustion, often feeling like her efforts are not enough despite trying hard. (Verbatim: "i'm trying so hard and it makes me sad to think that even if i try it's not enough sometimes") [end of text]



1. She has two older brothers and was often dressed in boy clothes as a child. (Verbatim: "when you already have two brothers, it just makes more sense to just put her in boy clothes, you know, like, yeah, no long hair, because it was difficult to take care of")

2. She once had long hair but had to cut it short after nearly choking on it in her sleep. (Verbatim: "I remember really struggling to take it off, and I was, like, panicking... my hair had wrapped itself around my neck, and I was, like, choking in my sleep because of my hair")

3. She is a restless sleeper and tends to roll a lot during the night. (Verbatim: "I'm a roller, I don't think anyone would ever want to share a bed with me, because I just roll a lot, like, like a lot")

