2. She prioritized downloading Steam and VTubing software when setting up her new laptop. (Verbatim: "the first thing i downloaded was steam so that i could get vtube studio")

3. She is originally from the UK and currently in America. (Verbatim: "i'm in america" and "last time i forgot to try the... british one")

4. She prefers British Coca-Cola over American Coca-Cola due to the use of sugar instead of high fructose corn syrup. (Verbatim: "uk cola we straight up sugar" and "american cola... high fructose corn syrup i was like oh no")

5. She became ill with COVID-19 while attending an expo in America. (Verbatim: "i got sick too of covid" and "i look forward to going again")

6. She grew up in England and has nostalgic memories of McDonald's nuggets tasting like "old childhood nuggets." (Verbatim: "the mcnuggets in america tastes like how the mcnuggets used to taste in england")

7. She finds it strange that American frozen chicken products list "ribs" as an ingredient. (Verbatim: "why are there ribs in my chicken... what's chicken rib meat")

8. She expresses a desire to try a "comically big cup" like a Big Gulp in America. (Verbatim: "i want to get one of those comically big cups would you guys call it big gulp")

9. She mentions having a habit of quarantining herself when sick to avoid bothering others. (Verbatim: "i've just like quarantined myself to this... last thing i want to do is spread signal")

10. She associates her illness with feeling isolated, noting she’s used to being alone when sick. (Verbatim: "being ill I'm used to just being alone") [end of text]



